  Two bugs[0m[2m,[0m[2m one[0m[2m fix[0m[2m:
     
     **Bug[0m[2m 1 — Overs[0m[2melling (TOCT[0m[2mOU race)**[0m[2m: The[0m[2m original[0m[2m flow[0m[2m called[0m[2m `check_stock()`[0m[2m → `charge[0m[2m()` → `de[0m[2mcrement()`[0m[2m as three separate async[0m[2m operations. Under[0m[2m concurrency, 12[0m[2m coroutines all passed[0m[2m the[0m[2m stock[0m[2m check, then[0m[2m raced[0m[2m on decrement —[0m[2m driving[0m[2m inventory[0m[2m negative. The `[0m[2mdecrement()` method[0m[2m itself was[0m[2m also vulnerable:[0m[2m its[0m[2m `if` check[0m[2m and assignment[0m[2m were separated by a[0m[2m yield point (`[0m[2masyncio.sleep`[0m[2m).
     
     **Bug[0m[2m 2 — Ghost charges[0m[2m**: Because[0m[2m charging[0m[2m happened *[0m[2mbefore* decrement[0m[2ming, a[0m[2m successful[0m[2m charge followed[0m[2m by a failed decrement[0m[2m (stock[0m[2m ran[0m[2m out between[0m[2m check[0m[2m and decrement) meant[0m[2m the customer paid[0m[2m but got[0m[2m no item.
     
